Z||000000||Julian||07-23-2001||07:49 AM||||Looking to replace my radio with one that has a CD player.  However I want it to look "factory".  Does Pontiac make one that can just plug into the existing harness? Maybe Firebird? What year? My Fiero is a 1988 Mera.<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/meralogo.gif"> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||Old Lar||07-23-2001||12:22 PM||||I added a am-fm with CD from a 98 Grand Am.  I bought a wireharness  <A HREF="http://www.gmpartsdirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.gmpartsdirect.com</A>   for less than $20 that plugs the radio to the Fiero wire harness.  It was pretty straight forward replacement once tgowens told me the trick.  Fits right in.  Do a search on radio for more info.  Or check out the recent thread on mods.  There is a photo of my radio in the thread.||||reg||1
Z||000002||RossT||07-23-2001||05:01 PM||||Do a search of the forum in both tech and general area using "up3" in the search. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||07-23-2001||05:17 PM||||Try <A HREF="http://www.aatechnologies.com" TARGET=_blank>here</A> or <A HREF="http://www.newellelectronics.com" TARGET=_blank>here</A>.  I think the last one has changed hands, but I can't remember the new URL.  Almost any DIN and a half size GM stereo from the late '80s on should work.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
